          %h2#representations_and_associated_bundles Representations and associated bundles
          %p
            The mathematical term
            %em group
            is short for
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                group of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetries"} symmetries
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the group of symmetries of some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is technically expressed by there being an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and this representation are suitably linear, this is also called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (namely a representation of the abstract group as an actual group of symmetries).
          %p
            The chapter
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+groups"} geometry of physics – groups
            discusses in detail how in geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            are equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            which have a single object and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
            of that object, if only
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
            via the canonical base point inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            This perspective turns out to be exceedingly useful for the discussion of the representations of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundles"} bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to \mathbf{B}G
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            that this encodes an action on is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of this map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  V &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; E
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In traditional literature this is familiar in special cases, where the perspective is usually the opposite: given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = \mathbf{E}G \times_G V
            which is associated to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
            via the action.
          %p Indeed, in the generality of geometric homotopy theory, this association is an equivalence, so that actions and universal associated bundles are essentially the same concept.
          %h3#model_layer Model Layer
          %h4#1RepresentationsOf1Groups 1-Representations of 1-Groups
          %p
            We discuss here ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groups"} infinity-groups
            which are just 1-groups), and their ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
            and ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundles"} associated bundles
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoids"} action groupoids
          %h4#ActionsOf1Groups Actions
          %p
            We discuss here traditional concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"} discrete groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acting
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representations"}> permutation representations
            ”) but phrased in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoids"} action groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} sliced
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            groupoids. The discussion immediately, and essentially verbatim, generalizes to pre-smooth groupoids and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            proper.
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(infinity,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-truncated+objects"} 1-truncated objects
          %p We write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_\bullet = (X_1 \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} X_0)
          %p
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object"} groupoid object
            given by an explicit choice of set of objects and of morphisms and then write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Grpd
            for the object that this presents in the
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to X
            (an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (regarded as a groupoid) and setting
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_\bullet = (S \underset{X}{\times} S \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} S)
          %p
            hence taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            as the set of objects and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            with itself over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as the set of morphism.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            presented by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet = (G \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow}\ast)
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            operation given by the product in the group. Of the two possible ways of making this identification, we agree to use
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi g
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ⋅
                              %msub
                                %mi g
                                %mn 2
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{g_1}}\nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{g_2}}
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \underset{g_1 \cdot g_2}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; \ast
                  }
                  \\,.
          #Action1Groupoid.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho \colon S \times G \longrightarrow S
            %p
              then the corresponding
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi S
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi ρ
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                      %mi S
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (S//G)_\bullet
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    S\times G
                    \\stackrel{\overset{p_1}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{\rho}{\longrightarrow}}
                    S
                    \\right)
            %p
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              given by the product in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              are the elements of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow } t
              are labeled by elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in G
              and are such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = \rho(s)(g)
          %p Schematically:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi g
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi g
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi s
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mn 1
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (S//G)_\bullet =
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \rho(s)(g_1)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{g_1}}\nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{g_2}}
                  \\\
                  s &amp;&amp; \underset{g_1 g_2}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; \rho(s)(g_1 g_2)
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For the unique and trivial
              = succeed "-action" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ast//G \simeq \mathbf{B}G
                    \\,.
          %p This makes it clear that:
          #MapFromActionGroupoidOnSetBackToBG.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              In the situation of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Action1Groupoid"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
